      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`test/registered/e2e/cp/test_cp_decode_attn_tp_server.py` was added in #46857 and has failed on every run so far: both targeted `/rerun-test` runs on that PR ([1](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41056533933), [2](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41094611156)), and every scheduled run since it merged:\n\n- [Oct 31, 4am PDT](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41195425101/job/124520624208)\n- [Oct 31, 4pm PDT](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41251070653/job/124684625363)\n- [Nov 1, 3am PST](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41300331378/job/124829869452)\n\nThe failure is identical each time: the first case (the fallback server with `--enforce-disable-flashinfer-allreduce-fusion`, 1-token prompt) fails the VERIFY versus teacher-forced CP prefill check with `Mismatched elements: 19 / 32`, max absolute difference `0.50715888` against `atol=0.02`. The greedy tokens match. Each failure also fails `extra-b-test-8-gpu-b300`, which hides the results of the other files in that shard.\n\n## Modifications\n\nSet `disabled=` on the file's `register_cuda_ci` call. `run_suite.py` skips disabled registrations, so the test stays in the tree and can still be run directly or with `/rerun-test`. Remove the `disabled=` argument to re-enable it once the mismatch is understood.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Registration-only change; no runtime code touched.\n\ncc @yuan-luo @BBuf\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41355030704](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41355030704)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41355030524](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41355030524)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41355030448](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41355030448)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
